  "id": "ca05a0da-1149-4547-883d-8012e76f09e8",
  "title": "Evolve to Learn: Gradient-aligned experience evolution for model self-improvement",
  "summary": "This study explores how self-evolving language models can continuously acquire useful experience through test-time interactions and prompts, yet challenges ensure that these experiences are effectively internalized into model parameters for self-improvement. The proposed framework, E2L, addresses these challenges by aligning gradient-based alignment with experience utility for optimal distillation.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "E2L iteratively generates, evaluates, and distills experiences according to their estimated training utility.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Gradient-based alignment is shown to be more reliable for downstream distillation gains than immediate test-time improvement.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "E2L closes the loop between experience generation and parameter learning, enabling agents to autonomously produce suitable experiences.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
